# Legal & Ethical Rules for My Cybersecurity Practice

1. I will test only my own lab machines, my own websites, or systems where I have written permission.

2. I will never scan, brute-force, exploit, phish, or attack public targets without authorization.

3. Before any penetration test, I must define scope:
   - Target IPs/domains
   - Allowed tools
   - Allowed testing time
   - What is not allowed
   - Reporting format

4. My job is not only to find vulnerabilities. My job is to document risk clearly and professionally.

5. For bug bounty, I will only test programs where I am enrolled and where the rules allow testing.

6. I will keep all evidence private:
   - Screenshots
   - IP addresses
   - Credentials
   - Reports
   - Client data

7. I will focus on defensive learning:
   - Vulnerability assessment
   - SOC monitoring
   - Reporting
   - Remediation guidance
   - WordPress hardening

